  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 230 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nTuesday-Sunday:\nA gradual warm up of temperatures through mid to late week, with\nthe jet stream displaced well to the north of the region. This\nwarm up will feature temperatures 5 to 10+ degrees above normal\nfor early October, with highs into the middle to upper 80s. At\nthis time, it appears we should remain a few degrees shy of any\nrecords, but it will be worth monitoring.\n\nThe warm temperatures will be accompanied by dry weather this\nweek and into next weekend. This includes daily minimum relative\nhumidity values around 20 to 30 percent, with localized lower\nvalues. Given the ongoing drought and minimal recent rainfall,\nfuels continue to dry out as we progress into Fall. This would\nsuggest the potential for localized elevated fire weather,\nthough winds remain a limiting factor this week.\n\nAs this pattern continues into next week, we may begin to see \nan increased fire risk as ensemble guidance hint at an increase \nin winds. This is particularly a concern with a frontal passage \nearly next week, which may be rather dry. At this time, there is\nstill remaining uncertainty on the extent of fire weather \nconcerns next week, but we will continue to monitor.",
